# Database & Migration Conventions

## Migration Files

Use golang-migrate. Files follow this naming:

```
backend/migrations/
  000001_create_users.up.sql
  000001_create_users.down.sql
  000002_create_guilds.up.sql
  000002_create_guilds.down.sql
```

- Sequential 6-digit prefix
- Descriptive snake_case name
- Every `up.sql` MUST have a corresponding `down.sql`

## Schema Conventions

```sql
CREATE TABLE guilds (
    id         UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    name       VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    icon_url   TEXT,
    owner_id   UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);

CREATE INDEX idx_guilds_owner_id ON guilds(owner_id);
```

Rules:
- All primary keys: `UUID DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()`
- All tables have `created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()`
- Tables that are updatable also have `updated_at`
- Soft-deletable tables add `deleted_at TIMESTAMPTZ` (nullable)
- Foreign keys always specify `ON DELETE` behavior
- Create indexes on all foreign key columns and frequently queried fields
- Use `VARCHAR(n)` with length limits for user input, `TEXT` for unbounded content

## Query Pattern (repository.go)

```go
func (r *Repository) GetByID(ctx context.Context, id string) (*Guild, error) {
    var g Guild
    err := r.db.QueryRowContext(ctx,
        `SELECT id, name, icon_url, owner_id, created_at, updated_at
         FROM guilds WHERE id = $1 AND deleted_at IS NULL`, id,
    ).Scan(&g.ID, &g.Name, &g.IconURL, &g.OwnerID, &g.CreatedAt, &g.UpdatedAt)
    if err == sql.ErrNoRows {
        return nil, fiber.NewError(fiber.StatusNotFound, "guild not found")
    }
    if err != nil {
        return nil, fmt.Errorf("guild.Repository.GetByID: %w", err)
    }
    return &g, nil
}
```

- Use `$1, $2` parameterized queries (never string interpolation)
- Always check `sql.ErrNoRows` separately
- Use `context.Context` for all DB calls
- Wrap errors with `package.Type.Method:` prefix
